## Abstract

Papers 1 through 3 of the **Afolabi Unified Framework (AUF)** formulated the substrate continuity (*Omi*), field excitation mechanics (*Afẹ́fẹ́*), and phase-coherence stability (*Ìwà*) of conscious entities (*Eniyan*). However, these internal dynamics require a formal cosmological geometry to explain where and upon what topological manifold physical observation occurs. This paper addresses the spatial architecture of reality by reinterpreting the foundational Yoruba cosmological axiom ***Aiyé l'ọjà, Ọ̀run l'ilé*** ("The physical world is a marketplace; the unmanifest source is home"). Moving beyond spiritual dualism, we formalize this axiom as a rigorous **Holographic Boundary Model** compatible with anti-de Sitter / Conformal Field Theory (AdS/CFT) bulk-boundary dualities. We demonstrate that physical $3D+1$ space-time (*Aiyé*) functions as a lower-dimensional projection screen—a transactional marketplace—derived from an $N$-dimensional quantum informational bulk (*Ọ̀run*). By formulating the mapping operator $\hat{\mathcal{T}}_{\text{Market}}$ and integrating a radial bulk coordinate $z$ into the complex metric tensor $\mathbf{\Omega}_{\text{AUF}}$, we provide a unified mathematical framework explaining state actualization, non-local bulk signaling, and the conservation of quantum state memory across dimensional boundaries.

