### 2.3 Holographic Area Laws and Information Density

The total quantum information capacity of a physical region $V$ in *Aiyé* is strictly constrained by the Bekenstein-Hawking holographic principle. The maximum entropy $S_{\text{max}}$ (information capacity) contained within a spatial volume in *Aiyé* does not scale with its volume $V$, but with the surface area $A(\partial V)$ of its bounding horizon in Planck units:

$$S_{\text{max}}(V) = \frac{A(\partial V)}{4 G \hbar} = \frac{c^3 A(\partial V)}{4 G \hbar}$$

